{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Independent seam review (2026-08-05) of the completion-recovery chain found: in\n`CompletionAgentStep._recover` (src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py),\nthe prelude `ticket = _reads.show_ticket(ticket_id, repo_root=ctx.repo_root)`\nexecutes inside the `except LLMBudgetExhaustedError` handler but BEFORE the\n`try:` whose `except LLMError` is the only place `self.failure_diagnostic` is\nbuilt. `show_ticket` raises `RebarError` (not LLMError) on a missing id or a\nstore that fails to reduce; that raise escapes `_recover`, `_run_leaf` flattens\nit to StepResult(status=\"failed\"), `failure_diagnostic` stays None, and\n`raise_completion_workflow_failure` takes the bare-LLMError branch: no gate\nerror sidecar, no aggregate_* keys — the primary run's already-computed budget\nand repetition diagnostic is dropped in full. Total evidence loss on a narrow\ntrigger.\n\n## Plan\nMove the prelude (at minimum the `show_ticket` call) inside the existing try so\na prelude failure lands in the `stage=\"preflight\"` arm, which already prefixes\nand preserves the primary diagnostic.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] A `RebarError` raised by `show_ticket` during recovery produces a\n      CompletionRecoveryError whose diagnostic carries the primary run's\n      aggregate_* repetition/budget keys (unit test, held-out).\n- [x] The gate-error sidecar is emitted on that path.\n- [x] The happy path and the existing recovery-failure paths are unchanged\n      (existing suite green)."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785982777497157001,"uuid":"815e02d1-c666-4494-9b2e-ca65efbabcc1"}